WEBVTT

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.900
What should I do?

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.610
Another dead end here?

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:38.770
How was it?

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:40.420
Useless.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:42.300
Just another dead end.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:43.570
That way too.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.230
Where the hell did they go?

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.520
It's pointless to hide! Come out now!

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.680
It's pointless to hang around here.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.750
Let's search somewhere else.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.380
Damn those annoying brats!

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.950
Maybe they didn't come out
because the scary lady was there.

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:09.930
Who are you saying is scary?

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.620
The lady... uh, gentlemen...

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.030
Mr. Porte!

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:37.010
Now I see, so that's how it was!

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:38.360
What happened?

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.710
I finally figured it out.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.310
...the reason the gravity control unit
wasn't working, that is.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:44.700
Really?

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:53.880
It seems the gravity control unit I brought was broken when we went through the gravity storm.

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:56.250
What do you mean?

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.800
Because of the effect of the gravity storm...

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:01.230
...the output signal of the phase-shift circuit...

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:02.880
..was being determined randomly!

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:04.650
Determined randomly?

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:05.880
Yep.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:13.610
And the Quark-Gluon controller's safety circuit was working, so it blocked the transfer signal.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:19.310
But the signal from the exotic controller
was amplified, so we didn't notice!

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:24.970
I don't really understand,
but the point is you'll fix it, right?

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:33.780
I'll have to get my hands into the output program and add some code to compensate, it'll take time.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.770
But you'll fix it, right?

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:36.860
Yeah.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:38.550
It'll go well this time!

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:40.870
You're not lying, right?

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.380
What reason would we have for lying?

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.380
Then you can really, really, really fix it?

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:47.280
Yes!

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.460
Alright!

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.320
Then we can go home?

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:55.270
We can at least get off this planet...

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:58.050
Alright! We can go home!

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:00.070
We can go, we can go, we can go home!

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.050
Howard! You're not well enough yet to get that excited!

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.600
As if I could keep my excitement in!

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:11.470
Alright!

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.870
We can go home, we can go home!

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.380
Hey, stop it, Howard!

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.930
We did it... We finally did it!

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.260
That doesn't mean you hafta cry.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.420
But I...

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:32.060
We can go, we can go, we can go home!

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.420
Now that's youth.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.880
We'll be home soon!

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:39.970
Home soon!

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.120
Kaoru!

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.670
What's wrong, makin' such a scary face?

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.900
Good news, Kaoru. We can go home!

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:50.360
We can?

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:53.250
It looks like we can get
the gravity control unit working.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.910
Although it might take a while.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:57.630
Really.

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:00.480
Great.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.300
How are things out there?

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.880
I can't even have any fun like this!

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:24.480
I wish something like a giant lizard would show up.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:34.230
They've been collecting topographical data?

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.360
Undoubtably.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:40.080
If they analyze that data,
they'll figure out the illusionary forest!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.030
They'll find the ruins!

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:45.780
If we could fix the gravity
control unit, we'd be fine.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.980
How much time do you think you'll need to fix it?

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:53.430
I won't know until it's done,
but maybe two or three days.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.560
Two or three days?

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.370
Can't you fix it any sooner?

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:00.630
If they find us before we get it fixed,
then all our work would be for nothing, wouldn't it?

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:04.160
I know that much without you telling me.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.330
Then fix it fas...ter...

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:11.580
Howard!

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:31.160
If we just wait while they search it,
they'll eventually figure out the forest's secret.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:36.300
The ruins are here, and the illusionary forest extends this far.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:40.120
In case they find this place,
we have to do something.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:41.320
It's true.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:44.550
How's Howard?

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:47.580
He seems to have calmed down.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.010
Good.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.780
Then, back to the plan.

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:53.850
There's no choice but to fight.

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:57.600
No way, Kaoru! They're not an enemy
we can beat face to face.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:01.420
Let's think of a way we can buy time.

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:06.070
Right here.

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:07.160
I see.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:52.570
Bob...

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.370
Did you figure anything out?

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:56.400
It's really weird.

00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:03.030
From the data we took from the ship about
this island, there shouldn't be a cliff here.

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:06.070
What's going on here?

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:22.120
Pague!

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.410
Pague!

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:27.670
I thought you'd be here!

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:32.400
Stop it, Pague! That tickles!

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:35.770
So? Have you been healthy?

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:47.880
You want to eat those, right? Give me a second.

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:08.400
Pague, it's unhealthy to eat so quickly!

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:14.470
Really, you're such a glutton!

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:34.160
I wonder where everyone's colony is.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:37.720
It's probably way further away than that star.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:43.800
What... should I do?

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:49.870
Luna, Menori, Sharla, Howard, and everyone...

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:54.780
...seem happy to return to their colony.

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:57.370
Well of course.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.920
It's their home, after all.

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:03.410
Luna says, "Let's go together,"

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:05.960
...but the colony isn't my home.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:11.320
My mom and dad might be on the mainland.

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:14.880
Things can't go on like this.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:18.300
If I could stay here with Luna and everyone...

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:20.550
...but that's impossible, right?

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:23.660
I mean, everyone has a real home waiting for them.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:29.100
Pague, what should I do?

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:37.120
Pague, you'll stay with me, right?

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:40.120
Whatever happens, you'll stay with me, right?

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:52.530
So Bell, you wait here.

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:53.620
Okay?

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.060
Okay, let's go with this!

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:58.530
I hope it goes well.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:01.080
We can't defeat them...

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:03.300
...but maybe we can delay them for a while.

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:06.110
And hope it gets fixed in that time...

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:11.320
It's okay!

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.050
They'll definitely fix it!

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:15.780
Anyways, let's start first thing tomorrow.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.710
Sharla, take care of Howard and Adam, okay?

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:21.970
Huh? Where's Adam?

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:25.270
Come to think of it, I haven't seen him in a while.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:28.460
I'll go look for him.

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:38.550
Adam!

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:40.610
Where did you go?

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:43.050
Outside for a bit...

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:50.400
Adam...

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:18.560
Well, should we get started?

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.110
Start with this tree.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.510
What's wrong?

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:36.180
Never mind. I just thought I heard something.

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:47.880
It's a perfect day for hunting.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:51.000
We'll find them today for sure!

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:51.820
Let's go.

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:53.320
Yeah!

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:03.600
Set a trap?

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:04.350
Yes.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:09.750
If they get past the illusionary forest,
we'll chase them into it and catch them.

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:15.900
We can't escape right now, and in the meantime we should be able to fix the gravity control unit.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:17.430
A trap, huh?

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:20.620
I would have thought of a better plan, though.

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:22.010
You've done it, Mr. Porte!

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:23.730
Alright!

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:26.850
Things are going well so far.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:38.020
Howard, are you okay?

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:40.650
Is it fixed?

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:42.710
As though it would be that easy.

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:44.360
You idiot.

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:47.920
What, just getting my hopes up...

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:50.850
But it looks like it's not broken as badly as we'd thought.

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:54.560
We may be able to fix this much by the end of the day.

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:56.280
Really?

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:59.170
Although it's just a possibility.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:02.770
So, outsiders should wait quietly over there.

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:06.370
Really? Fixed by the end of the day...

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:12.410
Sharla!

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:13.380
Huh?

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:20.470
You didn't have to run away.

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:21.900
But...

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:25.310
Fine, fine. I know I'm the pariah...

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:29.700
'tween gettin' excited 'n gettin'
depressed, he's a busy guy.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:32.510
Right?

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.330
Another dead end?

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:55.650
C'mon! What's going on on this island?

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:57.450
Let's check over there.

00:15:57.900 --> 00:15:58.420
Yeah.

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:01.230
Looks like they still haven't figured it out.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:09.220
Brindo, let's go!

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:10.870
Yeah.

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:22.160
I'll leave this here, okay?

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.810
We should connect this here.

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:28.080
You have to eat to stay healthy.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.000
That's amazing, Mr. Porte!

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:33.480
Did you see, did you see?

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:38.730
The miracles performed by I, the great Porte,
known as the galaxy's best mechanic!

00:16:39.030 --> 00:16:42.260
I'm inspired! To think you had such skills...

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:45.150
Huh?

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:47.880
Where's Adam?

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:52.910
Have you seen Adam?

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:56.170
Idunno. Isn't he playing over there?

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:06.260
Adam!

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.720
I wonder where he got off to?

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:13.120
I'm done.

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:14.550
I'm finished over here as well.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:15.300
Me too.

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:19.010
Then let's take a break for a while,
then start again in another spot.

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:20.360
Luna!

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:23.400
What's wrong?

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:26.400
Adam's nowhere to be found!

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:28.800
Did you look everywhere?

00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:31.650
I searched the forest all around the ruins.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.260
But he wasn't there.

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:35.360
Where could he have gone?

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:38.960
Bell, I'll go look for him.

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:40.050
Okay.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:43.350
Wait, Luna!

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:48.630
Where Pague is?

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.510
Yes, I have a feeling he's there.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:57.030
Adam...

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:00.220
Luna...

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:11.850
Adam...

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.120
If you can hear me, answer.

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:19.500
Adam!

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:23.960
Luna!

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:25.830
What happened?

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:29.770
Nothing. Let's go.

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:35.360
I don't know.

00:18:36.410 --> 00:18:39.000
I don't know what I should do.

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:46.680
There he is!

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:48.480
Adam!

00:18:49.570 --> 00:18:50.100
Luna!

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:57.330
Luna, are you okay?

00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:59.400
I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:01.530
Adam...

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:03.970
I'm glad you're safe.

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:05.130
C'mon.

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:07.010
Let's go back to the ruins.

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:08.020
I won't go.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:10.270
What do you mean?

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:12.820
Everyone can go back to the colony.

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:16.120
I'll stay behind here with Pague.

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:21.670
Adam...

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:24.110
Sorry.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.810
We didn't realize how you felt.

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:31.570
Maybe we were a little too enthusiastic.

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:34.570
But now we know how you feel, Adam.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:39.260
We can discuss what we'll do once
the space ship is fixed as a group.

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:43.080
But for now, come with us.
We're going back to the ruins.

00:19:43.650 --> 00:19:46.830
No! I'm gong to stay here with Pague!

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:51.930
Adam...

00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:02.280
Where could they be hiding that we'd
find nothing after searching all this time?

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:18.330
Hey, look at that!

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:19.720
Is it them?

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:22.610
We'll make that our dinner for tonight.

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.300
There's plenty there for all of us.

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:27.030
I'll grill him with my toy here.

00:20:27.260 --> 00:20:30.710
Idiot! Meat's best when it's raw!

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:33.260
I'll kill it in one shot with this.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:42.410
Luna...

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:44.510
Why are they in a place like that?

00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:47.320
Crap, what do I do?

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:56.960
What do I do? What should I do?

00:21:11.550 --> 00:21:13.570
So you've finally shown your face!

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:17.880
If you think you can kill us with that,
you've got another thing coming!

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:19.720
Kaoru's been spotted!

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:23.550
He's decoying them to save us.

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:25.950
Let's run while we have the chance.

00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:29.320
Cheeky brat!

00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:31.350
We won't let you escape!

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:35.960
Why did he reveal himself?

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:48.820
Where's he gone off to?

00:21:50.550 --> 00:21:52.980
The kid's got a set of legs on him.

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:06.300
Hey, hey! It's me!

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:09.150
What, just you?

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:11.920
I've solved the dead end riddle.

00:22:18.750 --> 00:22:20.430
They disappeared past here?

00:22:20.850 --> 00:22:22.200
What does it mean?

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:27.300
This cliff is an illusion -- a facade to stop us from passing.

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:28.570
Facade?

00:22:28.650 --> 00:22:30.900
Do you think we're idiots?

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:32.100
Just watch.

00:22:34.230 --> 00:22:35.510
Brindo!

00:22:39.450 --> 00:22:40.460
He disappeared!

00:22:41.020 --> 00:22:43.350
I see, that's how it was.

00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:45.260
Let's go too!

00:22:50.210 --> 00:22:52.830
Wait for me!

00:22:54.710 --> 00:22:57.180
D-- damn it!

00:23:03.330 --> 00:23:06.220
Crap! They made it past the illusionary forest!

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:08.770
'n we were so close to fixin' the space ship!

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:12.520
In that case, we'll all just have to
stall for time, just like we planned!

00:23:12.860 --> 00:23:15.110
But regular tricks won't work on them.

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:17.280
We won't know unless we try!

00:23:17.700 --> 00:23:18.820
Never give up!

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:21.750
You're right! Life's a struggle!

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:24.150
(But on the inside I'm terrified.)

00:23:25.350 --> 00:23:28.650
Next time: We can definitely do it.
